      "Run it as a randomised pilot on new subscribers only, not a network rollout; the intervention bundles three changes, so either factorialise them or stage them so the effect can be attributed.",
      "Agree with operations who owns the Ashby 88.7% reliability gap (PE6) so the same work is not funded twice as a retention initiative.",
      "Obtain a finance view before starting: if re-routing or confirmed-selection sourcing raises cost per retained subscriber, approval is required before the pilot begins.",
      "Fund the payment-failure instrumentation and the two cross-tabs in parallel (ALT-6 slices), with a decision review booked for the next quarter.",
      "Accept a weekly read-out cadence: warehouse data arrives in a weekly batch and same-week measurement is not possible.",
      "Protect the winter gifting pilot's Pell capacity in November and December when planning re-routed first-box volume.",
      "Report churn under both the pre-2026 and current pause definitions during the pilot so the result is not confounded by the reporting change."
    ],
    "tradeoffs": [
      {
        "id": "T1",
        "description": "Choosing the first-box fix means acting on the second-largest cancellation channel while the largest one stays unmeasured for another quarter.",
        "gains": ["An intervention that can start now with existing operational levers", "Direct focus on the day 0-21 cohort named in the desired outcome", "No new processor, no AI governance load"],
        "gives_up": ["Progress on the 47.2% payment-lapse channel this quarter", "The chance that instrumentation would have revealed a cheaper, larger win"],
        "alternative_ids": ["ALT-2", "ALT-6"]
      },
      {
        "id": "T2",
        "description": "Re-routing first boxes away from Ashby trades new-subscriber experience against Ashby's volume ramp.",
        "gains": ["First boxes served by sites running at 97.4% and 97.9% on-time"],
        "gives_up": ["Ashby's default new-subscriber volume, which was the mechanism for building the site up"],
        "alternative_ids": ["ALT-1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "T3",
        "description": "Declining the recommender and the menu widening disappoints two senior stakeholders whose positions are, on this evidence, preferences rather than findings.",
        "gains": ["Avoids a five-to-seven week processor assessment, an unbounded human-review obligation, and a capacity conflict with the 18-recipe Ashby cap"],
        "gives_up": ["CMO and Head of Culinary alignment in the short term", "Any upside if the vendor's unverified 18% claim happens to be real"],
        "alternative_ids": ["ALT-3", "ALT-4"]
      }
    ],
    "experiment": {
      "id": "EXP-1",
      "hypothesis": "For new subscribers, a first box fulfilled by Rowan or Pell, with starter-menu ingredients ordered against confirmed selections and an active prompt to choose before the Thursday 18:00 cutoff, raises day-21 retention above the 62.0% 2026-Q2 cohort baseline without raising the cost-per-retained-subscriber index above 100.0.",
      "method": "Randomise incoming new subscribers to control (current default: Ashby routing, forecast-ordered starter ingredients, no prompt) and treatment. Where engineering capacity allows, run a 2x2 on routing versus choice-prompt so the substitution effect and the choice effect can be separated; otherwise stage the choice-prompt arm second. Stratify by acquisition offer so discount depth does not confound the arms. Analyse day-7 and day-21 retention on the intent-to-treat population, with day-90 read later. Report churn under both pause definitions.",
      "duration": "8 weeks of enrolment plus a 3-week measurement tail for day-21 read-out; weekly read-outs only, because warehouse data arrives in a weekly batch and same-week measurement is not possible. Day-90 read follows roughly three months after enrolment closes.",
      "metrics": [
        {
          "name": "new_subscriber_day_21_retention",
          "role": "success",
          "definition": "Share of the randomised new-subscriber cohort still active at day 21, under the current churn definition and also restated with pauses counted as cancellations.",
          "target": "Treatment arm materially above the 2026-Q2 cohort baseline of 62.0%, with the effect distinguishable from noise at the pilot's sample size.",
          "rationale": "62.0% is the most recent measured day-21 cohort figure and sits inside the window where 62.4% of cancellations now occur."
        },
        {
          "name": "first_box_substitution_rate",
          "role": "success",
          "definition": "Share of first boxes with at least one item substitution, treatment versus control.",
          "target": "Treatment arm moving from the current 9.6% toward the 3.9% subsequent-box rate.",
          "rationale": "Operations attribute first-box substitution to forecast-ordered starter ingredients; this is the mechanism the sourcing change is meant to fix."
        },
        {
          "name": "menu_choice_made_before_cutoff (new subscribers)",
          "role": "success",
          "definition": "Share of new subscribers in each arm who make a menu selection before the Thursday 18:00 cutoff for their first box.",
          "target": "Treatment arm materially above control; the reference gap in the base data is 38.2% among 7-day cancellers versus 81.7% among day-90 retained.",
          "rationale": "Confirms the prompt actually changes behaviour, independently of whether behaviour change moves retention."
        },
        {
          "name": "cost_per_retained_subscriber_index",
          "role": "guardrail",
          "definition": "The existing programme index, computed for the treatment arm.",
          "target": "No increase above the 2026-Q2 value of 100.0; any increase triggers the finance approval gate before continuing.",
          "rationale": "Named in the FY26 objectives as the binding constraint on the programme."
        },
        {
          "name": "network_on_time_delivery",
          "role": "guardrail",
          "definition": "On-time delivery across all sites during the pilot, plus Ashby's own rate.",
          "target": "Network stays at or above the 95% service standard; Ashby's rate does not deteriorate below its 88.7% baseline as its volume mix changes.",
          "rationale": "Re-routing first-box volume must not degrade service for the existing base or stall the Ashby ramp."
        },
        {
          "name": "ingredient_waste_percent",
          "role": "guardrail",
          "definition": "Waste as a share of ingredient cost during the pilot.",
          "target": "No material rise above the current 4.1%.",
          "rationale": "Ordering starter ingredients against confirmed selections changes the sourcing pattern that the committed-volume agreement is built on."
        },
        {
          "name": "pause_rate",
          "role": "guardrail",
          "definition": "Share of active subscribers pausing per month in each arm.",
          "target": "No increase relative to the 3.4% Q2 rate that would make the retention gain a reclassification rather than a real one.",
          "rationale": "Paused subscribers count as active under the current definition and 61% of the Q1 paused cohort cancelled within 90 days, so pause can absorb a retention 'win'."
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

